      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{643c3899019a7db54e689337|full_name}: most crashes for VRChat on Quest are due to out of memory errors. The headset has 6 gigabytes of RAM. \n\nRight now there is a hard limit in the avatar SDK, for an avatar to be uploaded to VRChat the compressed avatar bundle must be less than 10 MB.\n\nIn a way that can limit the RAM usage of an avatar, so increasing it would allow avatars to use more RAM, making running out easier to do. \n\nMaybe it won't make things much worse, but this change won't make things better for Quest users running out of ram.\n\nWith server side stats in the pipeline, personally I'd like the hard cap to be based on uncompressed asset bundle size.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
