      "value": "@{631b62893d6ecd44ad392231|full_name}: I am curious about how you were using VRChat. Really small groups? Only looking at the bigger avatars in private?\n\nEven with avatars now 100% limited 10MB Quest standalone crashes often.\n\nWherever I see my quest friends in models that on PC are hundreds of thousands of polygons and like 20-40 materials I like to ask about the quest stats, and compare notes on what works. There has been a few times where there is like one toggle missing, so the quest polygon count is 40k less. But the rest is all there. \n\nAnother time there was a nice shield design and the quest version had half the pixels. \n\nOverall I believe VRChat needs to offer up something to encourage avatar creators to reduce the polygon count. I recently saw an avatar with a katana that was obviously kitbashed from three models, the blade was clearly ps2 era, a small area connecting blade to handle, covering the base of the blade had enough polygons to be used in a 3D film, and the handle had an inbetween amount. On the positive side I'm confident that both Quest and PC see the same polygons for that sword.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
